.TH VIRCON2PNG 1 "October 11, 2026" "Vircon32 DevTools 26.04.24" "Vircon32 Development Tools"
.SH NAME
vircon2png \- convert a Vircon32 texture back into a PNG image
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vircon2png
.RB [ \-o
.IR output.png ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.I input.vtex
.br
.B vircon2png
.B \-\-help
.br
.B vircon2png
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vircon2png
reads a VTEX texture (as made by
.BR png2vircon (1)
or extracted from a cartridge by
.BR unpackrom (1))
and writes it as an 8-bit RGBA PNG image. The texture must be between
1 by 1 and 1024 by 1024 pixels, and its file size must match the
dimensions in its header.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " output.png"
Write the image to
.IR output.png .
Without
.BR \-o ,
the output path is the input path with its extension replaced by
.IR .png .
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose: report the texture size and each step.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and author, and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The image was written.
.TP
.B 1
Any error, printed as
.IR "vircon2png: error: description" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR png2vircon (1),
.BR unpackrom (1)
.SH AUTHOR
The Vircon32 PNG extractor was written by Javier Carracedo
.RI ( Carra ).
This manual page was written by Matthew Haas for the v32c++ project.
